      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense, it's just a lot of pressure. one thing that's worrying me is the unpredictability of the actual border staff. i've heard stories about officials being super strict or even making things difficult for no reason at all, just by being difficult about paperwork or rules. is there anything we can do to prepare the team for those kinds of \"gatekeeper\" encounters or any common pitfalls where a small mistake in how they present themselves might trigger a rejection? i just want to minimize any friction with the officials at the checkpoints.",
